1
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:42,000
History is about to change

2
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:18,000
Colette is a drama, history film directed by Wash Westmoreland.

3
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:54,000
After marrying a successful Parisian writer known commonly as Willy, Sidonie-Gabrielle Colette is transplanted
from her childhood home in rural France to the intellectual and artistic splendor of Paris.

4
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Soon after, Willy convinces Colette to ghostwrite for him.

5
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
She pens a semi-autobiographical novel about a witty and brazen country girl
named Claudine, sparking a bestseller and a cultural sensation.

6
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
After its success, Colette and Willy become the talk of Paris and
their adventures inspire additional Claudine novels.

7
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:18,000
Colette, played by Keira Knightley.

8
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:54,000
Willy, played by Dominic West.

9
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
Missy, played by Denise Gough.

10
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Sido, played by Fiona Shaw.

11
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
Jules, played by Robert Pugh.

12
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
Georgie Raoul-Duval, played by Eleanor Tomlinson.

13
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
Colette is a 2018 biographical drama film directed by Wash Westmoreland, from a screenplay by Westmoreland,
Rebecca Lenkiewicz and Richard Glatzer, based upon the life of the French novelist Colette.

14
01:18:24,000 --> 01:18:30,000
It stars Keira Knightley, Dominic West, Eleanor Tomlinson, and Denise Gough.

15
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
It had its world premiere at the Sundance Film Festival on January 20, 2018.

16
01:29:36,000 --> 01:29:42,000
It was released in the United States on September 21,
2018, by Bleecker Street and 30West.

17
01:35:12,000 --> 01:35:18,000
The film premiered in London at the BFI London Film Festival and was
released in the United Kingdom on January 11, 2019, by Lionsgate.

18
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
The film explores themes of paris, france, nobel
prize, biography, author, 19th century.

19
01:46:24,000 --> 01:46:30,000
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
